17] [17592186050799 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186105795 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050799 #edb/ref 1031 "Permutations With Repetition" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050799 #edb/ref 1033 1341 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050799 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "67c9e5d0-cad6-5ae0-adf3-6535117a7d00" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051013 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049354 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051013 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186054672 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051013 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186054673 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051013 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186054674 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051013 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186054689 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051013 #edb/ref 1031 "Computing Probabilities Using Combinatorics" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051013 #edb/ref 1033 132 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051013 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "79d52f6b-aedf-5a99-b881-b489d9e71e06" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083024 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5676" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083024 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose a teacher needs to select a group of $4$ students from a class of $20$ students to represent the class in a competition. How many different ways can the teacher form a team of $4$ students?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083024 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e03fa018-0d27-5038-8c77-cf6bb723f9cf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083024 #edb/ref 1074 "The number of combinations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_nC_r = \\dfrac{n!}{(n-r)!r!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $20$ students, so $n=20.$ We want to select $4$ of those students to form a group, so we have $r=4.$\n\nTherefore, the number of different ways in which the teacher can form the team is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{20}{C}_{4} & =\\frac{20!}{(20-4)!4!} \\\\  & =\\frac{20!}{16!4!} \\\\  & =\\frac{20\\cdot 19\\cdot 18\\cdot 17\\cdot \\cancel{16!}}{\\cancel{16!}4!} \\\\  & =\\frac{116\\,280}{24} \\\\  & =4\\,845.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083025 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5677" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083025 #edb/ref 1071 "There are $10$ employees in a company, and $3$ of them are to be selected to form a committee. How many different selections are possible?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083025 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e87f2616-514d-5b27-9f41-055c1f32f0cf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083025 #edb/ref 1074 "The number of combinations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_nC_r = \\dfrac{n!}{(n-r)!r!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $10$ employees, so $n=10.$ We want to select $3$ of those employees to form a committee, so we have $r=3.$\n\nTherefore, the number of different ways to form the committee is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{n}{C}_{r} & ={}_{10}{C}_{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{10!}{(10-3)!3!} \\\\  & =\\frac{10!}{7!3!} \\\\  & =\\frac{10\\cdot 9\\cdot 8\\cdot \\cancel{7!}}{\\cancel{7!}3!} \\\\  & =\\frac{720}{6} \\\\  & =120.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083031 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5723" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083031 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate ${}_{7}C_5.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083031 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2c61e1e6-58d0-56dd-a63d-29bd5239add1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083031 #edb/ref 1074 "The number of combinations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_nC_r = \\dfrac{n!}{(n-r)!r!}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=7$ and $r=5,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\require{cancel}\n\t\\eqalign{\n                            {}_{7}C_5 &= \\dfrac {7!} {(7 - 5)!5!} \\[5pt]\n                            &= \\dfrac {7!} {2!5!} \\[5pt]\n                            &= \\dfrac {7 \\cdot 6 \\cdot \\cancel{5!}} {2!\\cancel{5!}} \\[5pt]\n                            &= \\dfrac {7 \\cdot 6 } {2 \\cdot 1 } \\[5pt]\n \t\t\t    & = \\dfrac {42}{2} \\[5pt]\n                            &= 21.\n\t}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083112 #edb/ref 1069 "e-7458" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083112 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate $(\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned})$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083112 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bafe3204-ab4c-5db4-ba21-b979e3090cd5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083112 #edb/ref 1074 "First, note that $\\displaystyle{{12}\\choose{10}}$ means the same thing as $_{12}C_{10}.$\n\n In general, the number of combinations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_nC_r = \\dfrac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=12$ and $r=10,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\require{cancel}\n\t\\eqalign{\n                            _{12}C_{10} &= \\dfrac {12!} {(12 - 10)!10!} \\[5pt]\n                            &= \\dfrac {12!} {2!10!} \\[5pt]\n                            &= \\dfrac {12 \\cdot 11 \\cdot \\cancel{10!}} {2!\\cdot\\cancel{10!}} \\[5pt]\n                            &= \\dfrac {12 \\cdot 11} {2} \\[5pt]\n \t                            &= 66.\n\t}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083224 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186083574 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083224 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186083580 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083224 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186233621 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083224 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256661 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083224 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256662 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083224 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256663 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083224 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256664 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083224 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186284768 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083224 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186332935 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083224 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186332936 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083224 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186389818 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083224 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186392770 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083224 #edb/ref 1039 "Calculating the Number of Combinations of Objects Chosen From a Group of at Least Ten" #e